# Anything listed here is invisible to "docker build", which matters for two
# separate reasons.
#
# Secrets: COPY . . would otherwise bake .env into an image layer, where the
# Mongo URI and the Gemini key stay readable by anyone who pulls the image.
# The real .env is handed over at run time with --env-file instead.
#
# Speed: node_modules is the largest thing in this folder and the image builds
# its own copy with npm ci anyway. The scratch folders are rebuilt at startup.

node_modules
npm-debug.log*

.env
.env.*

codes/
outputs/

.DS_Store
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Problem content stays out of the image on purpose.
#
# The image is the compiler and judge engine. Problems are content: they live in
# MongoDB now, and their test files live under testdata/. Content changes far
# more often than the engine does, and a published image holding test data would
# hand the hidden cases to anyone who pulls it.
#
# testdata/ is mounted at run time instead:
#   -v "$(pwd)/testdata:/app/testdata:ro"
# Read-only, because submitted code runs in this container and must never be
# able to rewrite the expected output it is being judged against.
#
# problems/ is the old file-based source, kept after the migration as a backup.
# Nothing reads it any more.
problems/
testdata/
